# Accessibility Standards - SLAM25 Project

## Core Accessibility Principles

This Poetry Slam members area follows **WCAG 2.1 AA standards** to ensure the application is accessible to all users, including those with disabilities.

## Semantic HTML Standards

### ✅ Proper HTML Structure
```html
<!-- ✅ Use semantic HTML elements -->
<main>
  <header>
    <h1>SLAM25 Members Area</h1>
    <nav aria-label="Main navigation">
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/participants">Participants</a></li>
        <li><a href="/rounds">Rounds</a></li>
        <li><a href="/news">News</a></li>
      </ul>
    </nav>
  </header>
  
  <section aria-labelledby="participants-heading">
    <h2 id="participants-heading">Participants</h2>
    <!-- Content -->
  </section>
</main>
```

### ✅ Form Accessibility
```html
<!-- ✅ Proper form labels -->
<form>
  <label for="participant-name">Participant Name</label>
  <input 
    id="participant-name"
    type="text"
    name="name"
    required
    aria-describedby="name-help"
  />
  <div id="name-help">Enter the participant's full name</div>
  
  <label for="participant-region">Region</label>
  <select id="participant-region" name="region">
    <option value="">Select a region</option>
    <option value="berlin">Berlin</option>
    <option value="hamburg">Hamburg</option>
  </select>
</form>
```

### ✅ Button Accessibility
```html
<!-- ✅ Descriptive button text -->
<button type="submit" aria-describedby="submit-help">
  Save Participant
</button>
<div id="submit-help">Saves the participant information</div>

<!-- ✅ Loading state -->
<button type="submit" disabled aria-busy="true">
  <span aria-hidden="true">⏳</span>
  Saving...
</button>
```

## ARIA Standards

### ✅ ARIA Labels and Descriptions
```html
<!-- ✅ ARIA labels for screen readers -->
<button aria-label="Close dialog" aria-describedby="close-help">
  <span aria-hidden="true">×</span>
</button>
<div id="close-help">Closes the current dialog</div>

<!-- ✅ ARIA live regions for dynamic content -->
<div aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true">
  <span id="status-message">Loading participants...</span>
</div>
```

### ✅ ARIA States and Properties
```html
<!-- ✅ ARIA states -->
<div 
  role="button" 
  tabindex="0"
  aria-expanded="false"
  aria-controls="participant-details"
  aria-describedby="expand-help"
>
  Show Details
</div>
<div id="expand-help">Click to expand participant details</div>

<!-- ✅ ARIA properties -->
<input 
  type="text"
  aria-invalid="true"
  aria-describedby="error-message"
  aria-required="true"
/>
<div id="error-message" role="alert">
  This field is required
</div>
```

### ✅ ARIA Landmarks
```html
<!-- ✅ ARIA landmarks -->
<main role="main" aria-label="Main content">
  <section aria-labelledby="participants-heading">
    <h2 id="participants-heading">Participants</h2>
    <!-- Content -->
  </section>
</main>

<aside role="complementary" aria-label="Sidebar">
  <!-- Sidebar content -->
</aside>
```

## Keyboard Navigation

### ✅ Tab Order
```html
<!-- ✅ Logical tab order -->
<form>
  <input type="text" tabindex="1" />
  <input type="email" tabindex="2" />
  <button type="submit" tabindex="3">Submit</button>
</form>
```

### ✅ Keyboard Event Handling
```javascript
// ✅ Keyboard event handling
const handleKeyDown = (event) => {
  switch (event.key) {
    case 'Enter':
    case ' ':
      event.preventDefault();
      handleClick();
      break;
    case 'Escape':
      handleClose();
      break;
    case 'ArrowDown':
      handleNext();
      break;
    case 'ArrowUp':
      handlePrevious();
      break;
  }
};

// ✅ Focus management
const focusFirstElement = () => {
  const firstElement = document.querySelector('[tabindex="0"]');
  if (firstElement) {
    firstElement.focus();
  }
};
```

### ✅ Skip Links
```html
<!-- ✅ Skip to main content -->
<a href="#main-content" class="skip-link">
  Skip to main content
</a>

<main id="main-content">
  <!-- Main content -->
</main>
```

## Color and Contrast

### ✅ Color Contrast Standards
```css
/* ✅ WCAG AA contrast ratios */
.text-primary {
  color: #1a1a1a; /* 4.5:1 contrast ratio */
  background-color: #ffffff;
}

.text-secondary {
  color: #4a4a4a; /* 4.5:1 contrast ratio */
  background-color: #f8f9fa;
}

/* ✅ High contrast mode support */
@media (prefers-contrast: high) {
  .text-primary {
    color: #000000;
    background-color: #ffffff;
  }
}
```

### ✅ Color Independence
```html
<!-- ✅ Don't rely on color alone -->
<span class="status">
  <span aria-hidden="true">●</span>
  <span class="sr-only">Status: </span>
  Active
</span>

<!-- ✅ Use icons with color -->
<button class="delete-button">
  <span aria-hidden="true">🗑️</span>
  <span class="sr-only">Delete</span>
</button>
```

## Screen Reader Support

### ✅ Screen Reader Only Content
```css
/* ✅ Screen reader only class */
.sr-only {
  position: absolute;
  width: 1px;
  height: 1px;
  padding: 0;
  margin: -1px;
  overflow: hidden;
  clip: rect(0, 0, 0, 0);
  white-space: nowrap;
  border: 0;
}
```

### ✅ Descriptive Text
```html
<!-- ✅ Descriptive text for screen readers -->
<img 
